  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Pre-multiplying both sides of the equation ${A}^{-1}B\\,x=d$ by $A,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1}B\\,x & =d \\\\ A{A}^{-1}B\\,x & =A\\,d \\\\ {I}_{6}B\\,x & =A\\,d \\\\ B\\,x & =A\\,d.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $B$ is not singular, it must have an inverse ${B}^{-1}.$ Now, pre-multiplying both sides of the equation $B\\,x=A\\,d$ by ${B}^{-1},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B\\,x & =A\\,d \\\\ {B}^{-1}B\\,x & ={B}^{-1}A\\,d \\\\ {I}_{6}\\,x & ={B}^{-1}A\\,d \\\\ x & ={B}^{-1}A\\,d.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
